# Provenance — charts/README.md § `SOURCE` is required, including when nothing was forked.
#
# ADR-010: "Their charts are a starting point, not a dependency. Where a chart is close, fork it into
# charts/ with the upstream commit recorded in a SOURCE file." Nothing was forked here, and
# `vendored: none` is an answer to "where did this come from" where a missing file is not.

vendored: none
upstream: https://github.com/strimzi/strimzi-kafka-operator

# The CRD contract these templates and CyberCloud.Providers.Messaging.Contracts render against.
# ⚠ Both halves must agree with KafkaClusters.KafkaKind and KafkaClusters.NodePoolKind, including the
# plurals — `kafkas` and `kafkanodepools` are what address a REST path, and neither is derivable from
# its kind.
upstream-api: kafka.strimzi.io/v1beta2
upstream-version: 0.45.0

# ⚠ WHY THE OPERATOR VERSION IS PINNED HERE AND NOT ONLY IN THE BUNDLE. Two facts about the CRD at
# this version are relied on in code and would be silently wrong against another:
#
#   * `spec.kafka` requires `listeners` and NOTHING else — no `replicas`, no `storage` — which is
#     what makes a node-pool-only topology a legal Kafka. Strimzi requires those two when node pools
#     are disabled, so a chart that also worked without the strimzi.io/node-pools annotation would be
#     a different chart.
#   * the CRD declares NO `default:` anywhere, so the API server's structural defaulting adds nothing
#     on write. KafkaClusters.Matches' remarks cite this by name when explaining why containment is
#     the right comparison for reasons OTHER than operator-side spec editing.
